<refentry xmlns="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xmlns:svg="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:ns3="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" xmlns:db="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook" version="5.0-subset Scilab" xml:id="parquetRead" xml:lang="en">
    <refnamediv>
        <refname>parquetRead</refname>
        <refpurpose>
            Read a Parquet or Arrow file and return a table/timeseries.
        </refpurpose>
    </refnamediv>
    <refsynopsisdiv>
        <title>Syntax</title>
        <synopsis>
            t = parquetRead(filename)
            t = parquetRead(filename, Name, Value)
        </synopsis>
    </refsynopsisdiv>
    <refsection role="arguments">
        <title>Arguments</title>
        <variablelist>
            <varlistentry>
                <term>filename</term>
                <listitem>
                    <para>Path to a Parquet or Arrow file.</para>
                </listitem>
            </varlistentry>
            <varlistentry>
                <term>t</term>
                <listitem>
                    <para>output argument - table/timeseries object.</para>
                    <para/>
                </listitem>
            </varlistentry>
        </variablelist>
        <para>
            Optional pairs <emphasis role="bold">Name, Value</emphasis> are:
        </para>
        <variablelist>
            <varlistentry>
                <term><emphasis role="bold">"RowTimes"</emphasis>, string/datetime/duration</term>
                <listitem>
                    <para> 
                        Time values used to define the row times of the resulting timeseries.
                    </para>
                    <para>
                        Accepted values are:
                    </para>
                    <itemizedlist>
                        <listitem>
                            <para>
                                a scalar string containing the name of a variable in the file,
                            </para>
                        </listitem>
                        <listitem>
                            <para>
                                a <literal>datetime</literal> vector,
                            </para>
                        </listitem>

                        <listitem>
                            <para>
                                a <literal>duration</literal> vector.
                            </para>
                        </listitem>
                    </itemizedlist>
                    <para>
                        If a variable name is specified, the selected variable must contain datetime or duration values.
                        It becomes the time vector of the timeseries and is removed from the data variables.
                    </para>
                    <para/>
                </listitem>
            </varlistentry>
            <varlistentry>
                <term><emphasis role="bold">"StartTime"</emphasis>, scalar datetime/duration</term>
                <listitem>
                    <para>
                        defines the starting time of the timeseries.
                    </para>
                    <para/>
                </listitem>
            </varlistentry>
            <varlistentry>
                <term><emphasis role="bold">"SampleRate"</emphasis>, scalar double</term>
                <listitem>
                    <para>
                        Scalar sampling rate used to build a regularly sampled timeseries.
                    </para>
                    <para/>
                </listitem>
            </varlistentry>
            <varlistentry>
                <term><emphasis role="bold">"TimeStep"</emphasis>, scalar duration/calendarDuration</term>
                <listitem>
                    <para>
                        specifies the interval between samples.
                    </para>
                    <para/>
                </listitem>
            </varlistentry>
            <varlistentry>
                <term><emphasis role="bold">"OutputType"</emphasis>, "auto" (default value) / "table" / "timseries"</term>
                <listitem>
                    <para>
                        specifies the returned object. If "auto" mode, <literal>parquetRead</literal> returns a table 
                         unless time-related options are specified.
                    </para>
                    <para/>
                </listitem>
            </varlistentry>
        </variablelist>
    </refsection>
    <refsection>
        <title>Description</title>
        <para><literal>parquetRead</literal> reads data stored in a Parquet (<literal>.parquet</literal>) or Arrow (<literal>.arrow</literal>) file.</para>
        <para>The imported data are returned as a <link linkend="table">table</link> by default.</para>
        <para>When time-related options are specified, or when <literal>"OutputType"</literal> is set to 
            <literal>"timeseries"</literal>, the data are returned as a <link linkend="timeseries">timeseries</link>.</para>
        <para>Columns stored as Parquet datetime values are automatically converted to <link linkend="datetime">datetime</link>
            arrays. Columns stored as Parquet duration values are converted to <link linkend="duration">duration</link> arrays.
        </para>
        <para> When <literal>"OutputType"</literal> is set to <literal>"timeseries"</literal> and no explicit time 
            information is provided, <literal>parquetRead</literal> automatically searches for datetime and duration variables 
            in the imported file.
        </para>
        <para>The first datetime or duration variable encountered is used as the row time vector of the resulting timeseries.
        </para>
    </refsection>

    <refsection>
        <title>Examples</title>
        <programlisting role="example">
        rand("seed", 0)
        x = ["a"; "b"; "b"; "c"; "a"];
        x1 = floor(rand(5,1)*5)-1.5;
        x2 = -floor(rand(5,1)*5)+0.5;
        t = table(x, x1, x2, "VariableNames", ["x", "x1", "x2"]);
        parquetWrite(fullfile(TMPDIR, "table.parquet"), t);
        t2 = parquetRead(fullfile(TMPDIR, "table.parquet"))
        // t2 = [5x3 table]
        //
        //    x     x1     x2 
        //   ___   ____   ____
        //                    
        //   a     -0.5   -2.5
        //   b     1.5    -3.5
        //   b     -1.5   -2.5
        //   c     -0.5   -3.5
        //   a     1.5    0.5 
        </programlisting>
        <programlisting role="example">
        rand("seed", 0)
        x = ["a"; "b"; "b"; "c"; "a"];
        h = hours([1:5]');
        x1 = floor(rand(5,1)*5)-1.5;
        x2 = -floor(rand(5,1)*5)+0.5;
        t = table(x, h, x1, x2, "VariableNames", ["x", "hours", "x1", "x2"]);
        parquetWrite(fullfile(TMPDIR, "timeseries.parquet"), t);
        t2 = parquetRead(fullfile(TMPDIR, "timeseries.parquet"), "OutputType", "timeseries")
        // t2 = [5x3 timeseries]
        //
        //    hours      x     x1     x2 
        //   ________   ___   ____   ____
        //                               
        //   01:00:00   a     -0.5   -2.5
        //   02:00:00   b     1.5    -3.5
        //   03:00:00   b     -1.5   -2.5
        //   04:00:00   c     -0.5   -3.5
        //   05:00:00   a     1.5    0.5 

        t3 = parquetRead(fullfile(TMPDIR, "timeseries.parquet"), "RowTimes", "hours")
        // t3 = [5x3 timeseries]
        //
        //    hours      x     x1     x2 
        //   ________   ___   ____   ____
        //                               
        //   01:00:00   a     -0.5   -2.5
        //   02:00:00   b     1.5    -3.5
        //   03:00:00   b     -1.5   -2.5
        //   04:00:00   c     -0.5   -3.5
        //   05:00:00   a     1.5    0.5 
        </programlisting>
        <programlisting role="example">
        dt = datetime(2026, 1, 1, 9, 30, 45):calmonths(1):datetime(2026, 12, 31);
        dt = dt';
        d = [1:12]';
        i = int32(d);
        str = "A" + string(d);
        b = [%f; %t; %t; %f; %f; %t; %f; %f; %f; %t; %t; %f];
        t = table(dt, d, i, str, b, "VariableNames", ["date", "double", "int32", "string", "bool"]);
        parquetWrite(fullfile(TMPDIR, "table3.parquet"), t);
        t2 = parquetRead(fullfile(TMPDIR, "table3.parquet"), "StartTime", datetime(2026, 6, 1), "SampleRate", 1/3600)
        // t2 = [12x5 timeseries]
        //
        //          Time                  date           double   int32   string   bool
        //   ___________________   ___________________   ______   _____   ______   ____
        //                                                                             
        //   2026-06-01 00:00:00   2026-01-01 09:30:45   1        1       A1       F   
        //   2026-06-01 01:00:00   2026-02-01 09:30:45   2        2       A2       T   
        //   2026-06-01 02:00:00   2026-03-01 09:30:45   3        3       A3       T   
        //   2026-06-01 03:00:00   2026-04-01 09:30:45   4        4       A4       F   
        //   2026-06-01 04:00:00   2026-05-01 09:30:45   5        5       A5       F   
        //   2026-06-01 05:00:00   2026-06-01 09:30:45   6        6       A6       T   
        //   2026-06-01 06:00:00   2026-07-01 09:30:45   7        7       A7       F   
        //   2026-06-01 07:00:00   2026-08-01 09:30:45   8        8       A8       F   
        //   2026-06-01 08:00:00   2026-09-01 09:30:45   9        9       A9       F   
        //   2026-06-01 09:00:00   2026-10-01 09:30:45   10       10      A10      T   
        //   2026-06-01 10:00:00   2026-11-01 09:30:45   11       11      A11      T   
        //   2026-06-01 11:00:00   2026-12-01 09:30:45   12       12      A12      F 
        </programlisting>
    </refsection>
    <refsection role="caution">
        <title>Caution</title>
        <warning>
            <para>This function converts data:</para>
            <simplelist>
            <member>float32 are converted to doubles</member>
            <member>date32/64 and ts are converted to datetime</member>
            <member>null booleans are converted to false booleans</member>
            </simplelist>
        </warning>
    </refsection>
